4806e7dc6cee4dca5dddfe82d","event_uuid":"418a731a-818a-491f-8951-7037e1ff3aff","position":{"commit_sha":"7610df0906b302a20272b33ca4198cbe3e27dd3f","position":"1786176554645125001-418a731a-818a-491f-8951-7037e1ff3aff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ecd3e8f41a9525d52d059be0e9de9cccc50ca72f631ca604309fbd1b9e8ae381","event_uuid":"0d0005a6-def6-4329-882c-a432516343e6","position":{"commit_sha":"7610df0906b302a20272b33ca4198cbe3e27dd3f","position":"1786176555168962001-0d0005a6-def6-4329-882c-a432516343e6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786047148272816001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d82959be-08b2-4807-a3b6-ab68825af4a8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"9ce8-8ff1-0832-4825"}],"description":"Scope: `src/rebar/_commands/**`, `_cli/**`, `_engine_support/**`, `_io/**`. ~205 lines leave.\n\nLargest cluster, unanticipated: the bash dispatcher is GONE (no `*.sh`, no `ticket_txn.py`) yet ~16 module docstrings still narrate 'Ports ticket-X.sh', 'byte-parity with the dispatcher arm', 'Tier E cutover', 'until E7'. ~126 lines, confirmed stale rather than merely historical. `docs/bash-migration.md` is the existing home.\n\nVerified stale and confirmed individually: `_commands/txn.py:3-8` cites a shim that does not exist; `_engine_support/reads.py:15-19` states a false reason for the module's location; `_commands/leaf.py:9-12` says tag/untag/archive are 'tracked as child tickets' while all three are defined in that same file; `_engine_support/__init__.py:7-9` cites compat shims that do not exist; `_io/__init__.py:14` says the import side 'lands in a later sub-task' six lines above the line importing it; `_cli/_help.py:3-8` is truncated mid-clause (introduced by 3a53e202a7).\n\n`_engine_support/reads_cli.py` explains the same unknown-option rule in five near-identical blocks — a ->CODE fix (extract one helper) rather than a comment edit.\n\nHeadroom: `_commands/init.py` 799 -> ~782 (18 lines of margin), `_cli/_llm_commands.py` 789 -> ~778 (22) — both WITHOUT any code extraction. The module-size pressure in these two files is partly caused by comments explaining previous module-size splits.\n\nNew ADR proposed: 'Explicit init over silent-implicit tracker creation' — a prior-art survey (git-bug/git-appraise vs git-issue/bugs-everywhere/Fossil) stated in four places.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criteria F1/E6)\n\nAC3/AC4 rested on a subjective correct-vs-delete judgment with no decision rule or observable\ncheck. Superseded below with the parent 373f disposition vocabulary and a recorded-reason rule\nfor every deletion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] Every substantial in-scope comment unit is dispositioned into exactly one of the parent\n      373f labels: RELOCATE (to docs/bash-migration.md, an ADR, or a ticket, reduced to a\n      one-line citation), DELETE, KEEP, DO_NOT_MOVE, or CORRECT-IN-PLACE.\n- [ ] Decision rule for CORRECT-vs-DELETE: a stale comment that documents CURRENT runtime\n      behavior / a live invariant is CORRECTED in place; a comment is DELETED only when the thing\n      it describes no longer exists (referenced artifact removed, or the statement is superseded).\n      For each DELETE, the reason (referenced-artifact-gone / superseded) is stated in the commit\n      body or a ticket comment, so no comment documenting current behavior is removed without a\n      recorded reason.\n- [ ] The dead bash-dispatcher narration (~16 module docstrings citing 'Ports ticket-X.sh',\n      'byte-parity with the dispatcher arm', 'Tier E cutover', 'until E7' — the bash dispatcher\n      and ticket_txn.py no longer exist) is relocated to docs/bash-migration.md where still\n      useful, or deleted as stale with the reason recorded.\n- [ ] The individually-confirmed stale comments are CORRECTED or DELETED per the rule above:\n      `_commands/txn.py:3-8` (cites a non-existent shim), `_engine_support/reads.py:15-19`\n      (false location reason), `_commands/leaf.py:9-12` (tag/untag/archive defined in-file, not\n      'tracked as child tickets'), `_engine_support/__init__.py:7-9` (non-existent compat shims),\n      `_io/__init__.py:14` (contradicted 6 lines below), `_cli/_help.py:3-8` (truncated clause).\n- [ ] The `_engine_support/reads_cli.py` five near-identical unknown-option blocks are collapsed\n      to one shared helper (behavior-preserving), verified by the existing CLI tests.\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands;\n      lint/type pragmas (`# noqa`, `# type: ignore`, `# ruff:`, `# tickets-boundary-ok`) and\n      test-introspected docstrings are DO_NOT_MOVE.\n- [ ] Any new ADR (e.g. 'Explicit init over silent-implicit tracker creation') EXISTS and is\n      committed before any comment citing it is collapsed.\n- [ ] The actual recovered comment-line count is measured (by diff) and recorded on this ticket\n      as an output, not a target.\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the full test suite AND `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass unchanged.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["depends_on","9ce8-8ff1-0832-4825"],["parent","373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","parent_status_uuid":"418a731a-818a-491f-8951-7037e1ff3aff","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"4fc1-dbde-6772-401f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: commands, CLI, engine_support and io","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["65259d30-fb9b-4810-8945-a8ca7e995837","d82959be-08b2-4807-a3b6-ab68825af4a8","cb8530c0-91be-4127-bdf3-ad8b377f859c","5737a44a-1443-49ed-ad46-ba34acb0b8f6","418a731a-818a-491f-8951-7037e1ff3aff","0d0005a6-def6-4329-882c-a432516343e6"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786176555168962002,"uuid":"a76f79e3-2f78-44b5-a8f8-4a27c268a630"}